{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/NoSQL Database.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/NoSQL Database.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"no sql database no sql database","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/NoSQL Database.md","fileName":"NoSQL Database.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"NoSQL Database","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-08 22:09\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Azure Cosmos DB Applications]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Azure Cosmos DB Applications","Document Database","c8andnetcore30projectsusingazure.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/NoSQL Database.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/NoSQL Database.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"no sql database no sql database","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/NoSQL Database.md","fileName":"NoSQL Database.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"NoSQL Database","heading":"NoSQL Database","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A NoSQL database uses a data model other than the traditional relational table-and-join model. The category includes document, key-value, graph, and other stores whose structures and scaling choices fit different access patterns.\n\nCosmos DB supplies a [[Document Database]] in the project, while its API compatibility lets the application use MongoDB conventions. Choosing NoSQL is therefore not merely choosing the cloud; it is choosing storage and query semantics that should match the application's data relationships.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Azure Cosmos DB Applications","Document Database","c8andnetcore30projectsusingazure.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/NoSQL Database.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/NoSQL Database.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"no sql database no sql database",